  "texto": "This will hurt. Because it's about you. You know it's destroying you. And still, you can't stop. This isn't love. It's addiction. Literally. Your brain doesn't lie. The same region that lights up... ...in an addict waiting for their next hit. Same circuit. Same hijack. You're hooked — and you don't even know it. And the worse they treated you... ...the stronger the pull. Not despite the pain. Because of it. It's called trauma bonding. That's why you forgive the unforgivable. That's why you check their profile at 3 AM. Again. And again. That's why someone GOOD bores you. Your brain calls it 'suspicious'. Toxic feels 'familiar'. Healthy feels 'wrong'. That's what the hijack looks like. This doesn't happen because you're weak. It happens to the strongest people you know. Because it takes strength to survive chaos. And that strength is your way out. Next time you can't stop thinking about them... ...say this: It's not love. It's your brain, drugged. And a drug can be quit. Comment 'THIS IS REAL' if you recognized yourself. And send it to someone who needs to hear it.",
  "voz": "en-US-JennyNeural"
